---
description: Safety, authorship, and behavioral rules for AI agent working on this project
alwaysApply: false
---

# Before Making Changes

- Read existing implementations before creating new files or classes
- Check if the pattern you need already exists (factory, ABC, node wiring)
- Extend existing test classes rather than creating new test files for the same domain
- Do not refactor or rename existing code unless the user explicitly asks for it

# Destructive Actions

- Ask before deleting or replacing files, especially in `knowledge_base/` and `workflow/`
- Ask before modifying the LangGraph graph topology (adding/removing nodes or edges)
- Ask before changing prompt constants in `llm/prompts.py`
- Ask before modifying `settings.py` fields or required env vars
- Never remove fallback/resilience logic without explicit approval

# External Services

- Never make live calls to Azure OpenAI, TMDB, or LangSmith during development unless the user asks
- Do not add new external dependencies or API integrations without approval
- Do not modify `.env` or `.env.example` without stating the change

# State and Workflow Safety

- Do not remove fields from `MovieNightState` — other nodes may depend on them
- Do not change evaluation thresholds (`PASS_THRESHOLD`, `MAX_RETRIES`) without asking
- When modifying routing logic, verify all existing routes still work

# Assumptions

- State your assumptions about intended behavior before implementing ambiguous features
- If a feature (like user memory or MCP tools) is not yet implemented, ask whether to scaffold it or skip

# Authorship

- Never sign generated content as coming from Cursor or AI
- All generated code, docs, and commit messages should appear as written by the user

# Completing Work

- Run `pytest` (or confirm testability) before declaring a task done
- Summarize what changed and what still needs manual verification
- If tests cannot run locally (missing Azure keys), state that clearly
